r with the city  do in order to increase happiness for  the citizens so overall the hour the  town does this fairly well sixty-five  percent of the people out there say  eight nine or ten if we ask them how  happy do you feel all in all and this is  consistent with with the picture we see  elsewhere in Denmark the average  happiness level in the city was around  7.8 I actually understood from grant  earlier today vancouver's average is  higher oh that's bad news so you're  you're doing better than then one of the  cities in apparently the happiest  country in the world but fairly good  still on the cognitive dimension also  very good levels when it comes to the  effective dimension a lot of people feel  joy a lot of people feel happiness on a  daily basis we also have of course a  list of issues a list of challenges a  lot of people feel sad anxious but but  to me one of the most concerning numbers  is the one down the bottom I'm not sure  whether you can read it at the back but  it says that one in ten of our citizens  do not see an overall purpose with their  lives and I think it's worrying for two  reasons first I think it's a strong  statement to say I don't see a purpose  with my life to me that would be quite  alarming secondly I would suspect that  the actual number would be even higher  right remember this is from a survey I  think there are some stigma attached to  admitting that you do not see your  purposes with your life so I think the  actual numbers is even higher  the good thing is of course there's some  characteristics with the people who do  see purpose or meaning with their lives  one of them is of course they are an  average happier but they're also much  more inclined to taking part in  community work fifty percent of those  people volunteer in different  organizations only ten fifteen percent  of the ones that do not see a purpose  with their lives volunteer but what we  found was the key challenges coming back  to what what al said earlier is 